llvm-3.7.1 patch: a thread-local with local linkage stays general-dynamic (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for a thread-local variable with local
linkage in position-independent code: it is accessed through the
general-dynamic model, not local-dynamic. It has NO UPSTREAM STATE: 3.7.1,
like every release from 3.8.0 to 12.0.0, gives a local thread-local the
local-dynamic model here, and no public PS4 rule is known. The evidence is
the executable's own (docs/DECISIONS.md D75): all 21,974 thread-local
accesses of the base are general-dynamic and none is local-dynamic, while
its four thread-local bools are read as masked single bits at 9,382
sites, the form GlobalOpt gives only a variable with local linkage (D74).
It is the 3.7.1 form of
tools/patches/llvm-4.0.0-tlsprot-02-local-tls-general-dynamic.patch.
4.0.0's tlsprot-01 is not needed: it restores 3.8's rule for a protected
symbol, which 3.7.1 has (only a local or hidden symbol is local-dynamic,
TargetMachine.cpp:120). Swept alone over the game module built by the
pristine 3.7.1 (round 270B, 5,496 rows, 6,641 functions): 424 functions
change; 246 rows become equal (4,789 to 5,035) and none is lost.

--- a/lib/Target/TargetMachine.cpp
+++ b/lib/Target/TargetMachine.cpp
@@ -117,7 +117,10 @@
 
   TLSModel::Model Model;
   if (isPIC && !isPIE) {
-    if (isLocal || isHidden)
+    // PS4: a thread-local with local linkage stays general-dynamic (the
+    // executable has no local-dynamic access, and its thread-local bools
+    // were local when optimised); only a hidden one is local-dynamic.
+    if (isHidden)
       Model = TLSModel::LocalDynamic;
     else
       Model = TLSModel::GeneralDynamic;
